    "probe_text": "The report is confirmed by the source. Here is the answer, in execution order.\n\n## `POST /api/owners` \u2014 validations and side-effects, in order\n\nThe endpoint is served entirely by an OfficeFloor function pipeline (`owners.POST.yml`), not a Spring `@RestController`. The starter dependency is present, so the pipeline is active. The whole file is guarded by `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`, so **the first gate is authorization** \u2014 no `OWNER_ADMIN` role \u2192 403 before any step runs.\n\nThen 18 steps run in this exact order. Note the body is bound with `@RequestBody` **but not `@Valid`**, so the JSR-380 constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size`) never fire \u2014 every check below is hand-written.\n\n### Validation / normalization phase (no transaction yet)\n\n1. **ValidateOwnerFields** \u2014 presence check: rejects with **400** (listing each offending field) if `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, or `telephone` is null/blank, or if `address` collapses to empty after normalization. Publishes the DTO for later steps.\n2. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 *(side-effect: mutates DTO)* converts telephone to E.164 (strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps `+CC`, else assumes `+61` dropping a leading `0`; requires 8\u201315 digits and a valid national length). Invalid \u2192 **400**.\n3. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 email optional; if present must match a regex (else **400**), otherwise lower-cased in place *(side-effect)*.\n4. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** \u2014 *(side-effect)* rewrites address in place: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET / RD\u2192ROAD / AVE\u2192AVENUE.\n5. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 postcode optional; if present must be 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD ranges) must fall in range, else **400**.\n\n### Transactional phase (`govern: [ transaction ]` spans steps 6\u201318; commits once at the end)\n\n6. **CheckOwnerDailyLimit** \u2014 counts existing owners registered on this request's business day (today, rolled off weekends); `>= 100` \u2192 **429**.\n7. **DetermineOwnerHousehold** \u2014 only if `sharesHousehold == true`: finds existing owners with the same last name + normalized address, derives a stable `HH-<hash>` id, and *(side-effect on OTHER rows)* **writes that household id onto every existing member and saves them**.\n8. **CheckOwnerIdentityUnique** \u2014 builds a consolidated identity key (`telephoneE164 | email | householdId`) and compares against all existing owners; match \u2192 **409**.\n9. **CheckOwnerCityCapacity** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); `>= 50` \u2192 **409**.\n10. **BuildOwner** \u2014 *(side-effect: constructs entity)* MapStruct `toOwner` (ignoring id and pets), then sets `registrationDate` to the rolled business day.\n11. **AssignOwnerHousehold** \u2014 *(side-effect)* stamps the household id onto the new owner if one was determined.\n12. **AssignOwnerCustomerCode** \u2014 *(side-effect)* sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (NNNN = count of owners in that city + 1).\n13. **AssignOwnerMembershipNumber** \u2014 *(side-effect)* sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`.\n14. **CountOwnerNamesakes** \u2014 *(side-effect)* sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name.\n15. **FlagOwnerBulkSignup** \u2014 *(side-effect)* sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if existing owners on this business day exceed 80.\n16. **SaveOwner** \u2014 *(side-effect)* persists the new owner via `ownerRepository.save`.\n17. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 *(side-effect)* logs id / customerCode / registrationDate to the `AUDIT` logger.\n18. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\n### Things worth flagging\n\n- **DTO bean-validation is dead code on this path** \u2014 no `@Valid`, so the `@Pattern`/`@Size` constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto` never run; only the manual presence check in step 1 applies.\n- **Step 7 mutates other owners' rows** (writing household ids) \u2014 a side-effect on records other than the one being created.\n- Steps 6\u20139 and 12\u201315 each call `ownerRepository.findAll()` and scan the whole table in memory, so the full owner table is loaded and rescanned several times per create.\n\nI didn't change anything."
